'''ankyloblepharon''' (ang″ki-lō-blef′a̤-ron), ''n.'' [NL., < Gr. ἀγκύλος, crooked (see ''ankylosis''), + βλέφαρον, eyelid.] In ''pathol.'', union, more or less extensive, of the edges of the eyelids. Improperly spelled ''anchyloblepharon.''

'''ankylose''' (ang′ki-lōs), ''v.''; pret. and pp. ''ankylosed'', ppr. ''ankylosing.'' [< ''ankylosis'', q. v.] '''I.''' ''trans.'' To fix immovably, as a joint; stiffen.

'''II.''' ''intrans.'' In ''osteol.'', to become consolidated, as one bone with another or a tooth with a jaw; become firmly united bone to bone; grow together, as two or more bones; effect bony union or ankylosis.

