'''Annamese''' (an-a-mēs′ or -mēz′), ''a.'' and ''n.'' [< ''Annam'' (said to be < Chinese ''an'', peace, peaceful, + ''nam'', south) + ''-ese.''] '''I.''' ''a.'' Of or pertaining to Annam, its people, or its language.

'''II.''' ''n.'' '''1.''' ''sing.'' or ''pl.'' A native or the natives of Annam; an inhabitant or the inhabitants of Annam, a feudatory dependency of China till 1883, when France established a protectorate over it. {{smaller|Annam occupies the eastern portion of the Indo-Chinese peninsula, having China proper on the north and Siam on the west.}}

